meta {
  name: Create Series
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/time-block-series
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Inglês toda Seg/Qua",
    "startDate": "2026-10-01",
    "endDate": "2026-12-31",
    "pattern": {
      "type": "WEEKLY_WEEKDAYS",
      "weekdays": [1, 3],
      "time": "09:00",
      "durationMinutes": 60
    }
  }
}

docs {
  # Create Series

  Creates a recurring series owned by the authenticated user and materializes
  its occurrences into time blocks up to min(endDate, today+12 months). Returns 201.

  Requires ACCESS_TOKEN cookie (login/register first) + X-CSRF-Token header
  (the `csrfToken` env var is auto-filled by the login/register/refresh
  post-response script — never paste it manually).

  Body: `title` (1–200, required), `projectId` (optional, must belong to the
  user else 404), `startDate` (required), `endDate` (optional, >= startDate),
  `pattern` (required): `type` DAILY | DAILY_INTERVAL | WEEKLY_WEEKDAYS | SINGLE,
  `interval` (>=1, DAILY_INTERVAL only), `weekdays` (non-empty subset of 0-6
  where 0=Sunday, WEEKLY_WEEKDAYS only), `time` HH:mm, `durationMinutes` 1–1440.

  Returns 400 INVALID_SERIES_PATTERN on bad pattern, 400 INVALID_SERIES_RANGE
  when endDate < startDate, 404 when `projectId` does not belong to the user.

  NOTE: the backend log line "Request without Origin and Referer headers"
  is a harmless WARN (fail-open for non-browser clients like Bruno) — it does
  NOT block the request. Real failures come with HTTP status: 401 = login
  first, 403 = missing/wrong X-CSRF-Token.
}
